+# The 19-locus arm — submitted 2026-09-03
+
+55 jobs (`63960585`–`63960649`), manifest
+`slurm_logs/manifests/submitted_20260903_160932_249070.json`. Reproduce with
+`submit_sd19.sh` in this folder.
+
+## Why it exists
+
+The run above rebuilt the tokenizer and measured it at **per-drug loci only**.
+Every 19-locus `locusfusion` number in the project — including the 0.9242 that
+`notebooks/claims.ipynb` quotes in Figures 1, 4 and A2 as this architecture's
+headline — therefore still comes from `newmodels_full/sd19_*`, which ran the
+**old** tokenizer, with katG S315's nucleotide token 43 codons away from its own
+protein token and an N call indistinguishable from a match.
+
+That gap is what this arm closes. `--arch` is not even different from its
+control; only the tokenizer underneath it is.
+
+## What it is matched to
+
+| control | what it holds |
+|---|---|
+| `newmodels_full/sd19_*__locusfusion` | the same five cells, same loci, same protocol, OLD tokenizer |
+| `alllocus_run_v2/all_modalities__mdcnn` | macro CV **0.9246**, the best established 19-locus cell |
+
+Same 300 epochs / patience 30 / `--min-epochs 50` / `--save-weights best` /
+seed 0, and a locus list pinned byte-identical to `newmodels_full/submit.sh`.
+
+## The canary
+
+Job `63960409` ran ISONIAZID × all four modalities × 19 loci at 3 epochs before
+the fleet went out, to check the rebuilt tokenizer on the real 19-locus input
+rather than on the synthetic fixtures:
+
+```
+CV AUC = 0.9644 +/- 0.0003 (2 folds, best_epoch=3)   TEST AUC = 0.9659
+COMPLETED in 00:09:18, MaxRSS 8.95 GB
+```
+
+No warnings, checkpoint written, the three implied flags all resolved
+(`per-locus branches`, `--delta`, `symbol-id variant tokens`). **MaxRSS 8.95 GB
+against the 64 G asked and the 128 G `newmodels_full` asked** — the int8 symbol
+ids are doing what `CODE_CHANGES_20260901.md` §2 said they would, and a future
+arm can drop the allocation further.
+
+`tests/test_locusfusion.py` passes 36/36 on this tree, including the
+real-alignment check that katG S315 lands on WHO codon 315 through both the
+nucleotide and the protein stream.
+
+## What to read when it lands, in order
+
+1. **Macro CV against `newmodels_full/sd19_*`.** Does the +0.0173 the per-drug
+   arm measured transfer? Judge it fold-paired: both arms use the same
+   `StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` on the same cohort.
+2. **Fold-paired difference against `alllocus_run_v2/all_modalities__mdcnn`.**
+   The per-drug arm tied `mdcnn` (+0.0003) and at 19 loci the old tokenizer sat
+   at −0.0004 [−0.0062, +0.0048]. If the +0.017 transfers, this is the first
+   cell in the project that beats the established architectures outside noise —
+   and the first thing that would let the project claim the tokenization is an
+   improvement rather than a parameter-efficiency result.
+3. **Read-out attention over 19 keys.** The per-drug arm had only 2 keys, so its
+   KL 0.0308 from uniform was a weak test. Nineteen keys is the real one, and
+   `token_signal`'s failure mode was attention pinned at exactly 1/n. Note that
+   `claims.ipynb` Figure 4 measures the OLD tokenizer's read-out at
+   1.06–1.11x uniform across 19 loci — essentially flat. If the rebuilt one is
+   still flat there, the locus selection is happening somewhere other than the
+   attention regardless of the tokenizer, and Claim 6 stands unchanged.
+
+## Where the outputs are
+
+**Written under the worktree**, not the main checkout:
+`.claude/worktrees/lf-token-offset-fix/biophysical-fusion/results/experiments/locusfusion_v2/sd19_*`.
+The main tree is still on the pre-fix tokenizer, so the jobs had to run from the
+branch that has the rebuilt one. Copy the finished cells across (or merge
+`worktree-lf-token-offset-fix`, which fast-forwards cleanly) before rebuilding
+`notebooks/claims.ipynb`, which reads the main tree's `results/`.
+
+## Not covered
+
+The five `md_multidrug_*__locusfusion` cells are still on the old tokenizer.
+That is a separate 5-job arm and it is not in this submission.
